  "transcript": [
    {
      "approx_t": 0,
      "text": "Think your lips are too thin? This is the mouth you're picturing."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 3,
      "text": "And it was never about size."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 5,
      "text": "Lips are not a feature. They are the line the lower face is measured from."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 11,
      "text": "Your eye never measures a feature alone. It measures the gaps around it."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 17,
      "text": "Move the lip line and every gap moves."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 20,
      "text": "One. The gap between nose and lip. Full lips make it short. Thin lips, long."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 27,
      "text": "The nose isn't what changed."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 30,
      "text": "Two. The chin reads stronger. The chin isn't what changed either."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 36,
      "text": "Here is that range, on one face. Watch the gap, not the lips."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 41,
      "text": "Now turn it. A front photograph hides it."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 46,
      "text": "None of this means fuller is better. It means lips are load-bearing."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 51,
      "text": "On many faces, less is the change."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 54,
      "text": "Do this now. Roll your lips inward and hold. Watch your chin arrive."
    },
    {
      "approx_t": 60,
      "text": "You will not get that mouth. See it on your own face first."
    }
  ],
